        "story": "A tailor takes a note asking for blue buttons on a coat. Before she finishes, the customer changes the order to red buttons. The tailor asks the blue-button helper to stop. That helper may already be carrying the buttons and may not hear the request in time. Each note has an order number. When a helper returns, the tailor checks the number against the current order before changing the coat. Blue buttons from the old note are put aside. Asking the helper to stop and deciding which delivery still belongs are separate jobs.",
