        "story": "A bicycle mechanic keeps a notebook. One page sketches how to repair a brake. Another records a brake she repaired on a practice bicycle and the checks she ran. A third says a colleague followed her notes and repaired another bicycle without extra help. These pages show different things: a plan, an executed check, and useful transfer to someone else. The mechanic labels each page and keeps the parts and conditions clear. A neat sketch is valuable, but it does not become a road-tested repair merely by being placed in the notebook.",
