        "story": "Ravi borrows a room to sort parcels. The caretaker can ask him to leave when the room is needed. Ravi writes down the unfinished parcel numbers so he can resume later. When asked to leave, he stops accepting new sorted piles and hands back the key once. A helper may still bring a pile prepared earlier. Ravi checks whether that job is still open before accepting it. A promise that the room might be free tomorrow is not a booking for nine o’clock.",
