        "solution": "\u003cp>Use the complete source as your starting point. Add \u003ccode>Text(\"Build note: synthetic fixture\")\u003c/code> after the second Text inside VStack. Change the greeting to Hello, Demo Lin. The new Text is the third text line, below the other two, with the stack's declared gap. You have changed the screen description. You do not need another startup callback, storyboard, or manual insertion of a platform view.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A good record names the scratch app scheme, Debug configuration, iOS 17 minimum, installed simulator name and runtime, and the observed three-line screen. Record Build's compiler outcome separately from Run's installation and display outcome. If only Build was performed, leave launch pending. The repository comparison should identify its App entry at the verified anchor and note its own manifest minimum and dependencies; it should not copy the company target's settings into the learner app. A correct explanation says that changing a Swift string affects a compiled source input, while choosing a simulator selects where a Run action executes.\u003c/p>"
