        "solution": "\u003cp>The first orange area includes twelve points around the text. The second leaves those added margins outside its orange area. InfoCard similarly adds padding, expands its wrapper, then attaches the background. For a vertical subtitle layout, replace the caller's HStack with \u003ccode>VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 8)\u003c/code>. Keep the Image and the text VStack, and remove Spacer. InfoCard's initializer still accepts this content because the replacement also conforms to View.\u003c/p>\u003cp>This variation is an explicit layout alternative, not an automatic size-class rule. Record the observed width and text size before selecting it for a product. Do not add .id(UUID()) to force a refresh or start work from the content closure; neither addresses content width. A useful worked answer draws Text → padding → background for the first comparison and Text → background → padding for the second, then explains why the card's internal title style does not require rewriting its caller's subtitle. Advanced alignment guides and custom Layout caching belong to later focused practice.\u003c/p>"
