        "story": "A repair desk accepts four phones. It allows two repairs to be active at once. When a repair needs an outside part, the clerk records where to continue and serves another customer while waiting. That is different from holding the counter closed until the part arrives. Polishing a phone also keeps someone busy even though it involves no waiting. The desk starts the next repair only when one active repair ends. Each phone keeps its numbered ticket, so the finished phones can be returned in ticket order even when repairs finish in a different order.",
        "meaning": "Suspension lets a task wait without occupying its current thread. Synchronous CPU work and blocking I/O occupy a thread until they return. A bounded task window limits child admission, and indexed results preserve input order. @concurrent leaves caller-actor execution; it does not create a private thread.",
