        "story": "Nora has a large photograph and four small desk frames. She prints four large copies and puts each behind a small opening. The visible pictures fit, but all four large sheets still take space. She instead makes four smaller copies sized for those frames. Before throwing the originals away, she checks that each small copy shows the required detail. Counting the paper kept on the desk and in drawers matters more than measuring just the frame openings.",
