      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Specify a whole-selection replacement and undo contract. Then choose one synthetic media or performance experiment with a result that could disprove the hypothesis.",
        "steps": [
          "Derive the emoji's UTF-16 range in A👩🏽‍💻éB from Swift indices. Predict the replacement and reject a fabricated interior boundary.",
          "Capture before and after selections for one-command undo and redo; state how native editing and marked text remain owned.",
          "Run the bounded Foundation snippet if tooling is available and retain exact output; keep UIKit interaction pending.",
          "Choose bundled playback, layer animation, GPU array addition or bundled-model inference. Define correctness, boundaries, device setup, work limits and a stop or rollback condition."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "Replacement keeps adjacent combining text and rejects out-of-bounds, NSNotFound and non-Character endpoints.",
          "The command restores text and selection once; provisional composition is not silently treated as committed text.",
          "The chosen branch names a bottleneck hypothesis, a correctness check and bounded work.",
          "Host string results, native editing behavior and physical-device performance remain separate evidence."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>Find the emoji's Character boundaries, then create its UTF-16 range with NSRange(start..&lt;end, in: text). Do not guess the joined emoji's storage length. Replace the whole selection with X to obtain AXéB, leaving the accent attached to e. Under this custom whole-Character rule, reject an endpoint inside the emoji even when representation conversion can produce an index. An out-of-bounds range or NSNotFound also returns no result. These are Foundation helper checks, not observations of an input method or native text view.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Capture before text and selectedRange plus after text and the collapsed caret. For this literal replacement, compute the caret in UTF-16 at the validated selection start plus the replacement's UTF-16 length. The undo action restores the complete before state and registers redo for the after state. Group only this custom command, label it Replace selection, and avoid registering a second action for the native text control's same edit. If composition is active, defer the custom normalization command or require an explicit committed edit boundary rather than silently replacing marked text.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For a branch example, choose bundled playback and hypothesize that delayed first frame is dominated by metadata load or decode. Define intervals for item creation/loading, readiness, first presented frame and pause/teardown. Preserve expected content, orientation, controls and interruption behavior as correctness oracles. Keep one player owner, release observers and bound concurrent preparation to the visible item plus a declared prefetch allowance. A future device experiment retains actual traces and conditions; this answer supplies no timings and claims no speedup.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A different acceptable choice is GPU array addition with a CPU numerical oracle and bounded in-flight buffers, or inference with labeled accuracy fixtures and separate preprocessing intervals. Choosing Metal merely because animation exists is insufficient reasoning. Document the evidence that would justify the branch, the simpler alternative and the point at which a specialist project takes over. Foundation compilation, UIKit interaction, GPU correctness, realtime audio and model validation remain distinct evidence rows.\u003c/p>"
      },
