      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Choose one packing-checklist feature using synthetic facts. Define its states, manual fallback, owner and evidence plan.",
        "steps": [
          "Compare watch acknowledgment, a spatial window, a Bluetooth counter and an optional health summary. Justify one and a simpler alternative.",
          "Write at least five transitions covering unavailable capability, opt-out, lost execution, old identity and recovery.",
          "Add the branch's failure case: lost watch reply, failed immersion entry, Bluetooth disconnect or malformed data, or ambiguous empty health results.",
          "Run applicable policy checks. Keep every unperformed NativeChecklist row pending."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "The choice names an observable user benefit, accountable owner, alternative and reversal condition.",
          "Availability, capability, consent, execution opportunity and data readiness remain separate inputs.",
          "Duplicate or old-owner input causes no new unintended mutation and the fallback stays useful.",
          "Host success is never treated as real transport, read authorization, wearer comfort or background execution evidence."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>The worked watch feature offers one Mark packed command and a latest checklist snapshot. The phone, or an explicitly chosen independent authority, owns the durable checklist. The watch owns pending presentation. Context updates carry document revision and replace earlier snapshots. Commands carry operation ID, item ID and account generation. The receiver must persist effect and receipt within its actual transaction boundary. After a lost reply, replay returns the stored acknowledgment. That retry preserves the original intention; a new tap representing another intention gets a different operation ID.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The state machine starts unavailable, ready, pending, acknowledged or recoverable failure. Unavailable support or product opt-out offers the ordinary checklist. Activated but unreachable transport queues the command without promising when it will apply. A reachable message attempts immediate delivery but still handles failure. On account rotation, old pending commands cannot mutate the new document. A duplicate acknowledgment may update pending presentation once but does not repeat the mutation. Background opportunities are used when offered, not converted into a promise of constant watch execution.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Compare this with keeping the action on the phone. The branch is justified only if the repeated task benefits from a wrist interaction enough to support pairing, delayed delivery and watch-specific UI. A trial needs actual user-task evidence and transport failure observations before wider adoption. Name the owner of phone/watch protocol versions and the owner of support recovery. If delayed pending state confuses users or counterpart support becomes too costly, the reversal path preserves the phone task and stops promoting the watch action.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Other branch choices are valid when they provide equally concrete contracts. A health answer must preserve No visible data without inventing denial. A Bluetooth answer must stop discovery and reject malformed payloads. A vision answer must provide system input and a window path on immersion failure. The supplied model verifies policy only. Target construction, signing claims, native interactions and physical-device evidence remain explicitly pending, and neither the worked answer nor passing example checks records learner completion.\u003c/p>"
      },
