      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Create an isolated app target and implement one original extension in a personal copy. Submit behavior and native evidence separately.",
        "steps": [
          "Add the four app files to a new scratch iOS 17+ target without the host @main file.",
          "Choose filtering or duplication, write its product policy and implement it without changing stable identities.",
          "Add an adversarial host case and run it with exact expected before/after state.",
          "Build and run the target when possible; check keyboard Save/Cancel, VoiceOver, largest text and relaunch; mark unrun rows pending."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "The source set has exactly one app entry and no company dependencies or credentials.",
          "The new behavior handles hidden or duplicated tasks by stable identity and has an independent failure case.",
          "Accessible actions communicate completion and editing separately; validation and save recovery are discoverable when actually tested.",
          "The ledger distinguishes passed host logic from native build and observed UI/runtime results."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>For the filter option, derive visibleItems from model.items and the local filter flag. Render visibleItems in ForEach, map deletion offsets through that same value, then call delete with IDs. Disable move while filtering. With A incomplete, B complete and C incomplete, visible A, C maps offset one to C. After delete, full state is A, B, so hidden B survives.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Add a host assertion for that mapping and another for editing C after deletion. The stale rename returns false and does not recreate C. Then inject a write failure during a valid change to A; the changed memory stays dirty, and retry persists the latest full collection including hidden B. These cases prove your extension integrates with the existing identity and failure policy.\u003c/p>\u003cp>In Xcode, keep generated and supplied entry points from competing by removing the generated target members. Build the actual macro-enabled source and record the target, destination, language mode and result. If macro expansion or runtime access is blocked, retain the exact error and mark the remaining rows pending. Do not use TODO_HOST in the app to convert a typecheck into an observation claim.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A native submission records separate observations for keyboard submit, Cancel, completion announcement, edit action, focus after deletion, wrapping at large text, and relaunch preserving ID/order. Source inspection can motivate those checks but cannot substitute for them. The handoff also names single-writer storage and synchronous I/O limits, supplies the independent diff and avoids claiming that reading the worked answer completed the learner's project.\u003c/p>"
      },
