        "solution": "\u003cp>Give Ember ID ember and symbol EMB. Searching EMB matches the symbol. With Favorites only enabled, it appears only if ember is in the set. Clearing query or disabling the filter changes derived rows without deleting the accepted Asset or preference.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Navigate by ember. When a valid replacement excludes that ID, the existing detail reports absence instead of substituting the next index. Retain the preference under this declared policy, so later reappearance makes it useful. No copied Asset remains silently stale while the catalog advances.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Build next before saving. Inject a writer that throws and verify previous favorites remain visible while catalog rows stay accepted. Corrupt-store initialization refuses writes rather than resetting bytes. Ordinary reopen establishes basic persistence, leaving crash and multiwriter behavior pending.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Repeated Ember seconds fail series validation before Chart. Valid samples keep Decimal amounts, converting only display copies. Record the changed fixture, expected filter/detail states, actual commands and any native interaction. Locale formatting and accessibility need observed settings and outcomes, not inference from compilation. This answer leaves independent implementation and evidence to the learner.\u003c/p>"
