        "solution": "\u003cp>Add Ember using the documented array schema, with no icon URL by default. Predict a matching symbol query, a Favorites only exclusion before saving and inclusion after success, then detail absence after an accepted replacement removes ember. A failed favorite writer retains the saved selection rather than changing it optimistically.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Create separate snapshot and resource gates. Capture their tokens, invalidate only the resource lane, and deliver its obsolete success and error. Both are rejected. The snapshot token remains current and its accepted rows stay available. Explain that this proves local authority separation, not that a remote server stopped sending bytes instantly.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Run the real service adapters through the offline protocol and compare accepted arrays. Inject an additional MIME or malformed-input case and record which boundary fails. Typecheck every native source against the selected simulator target. Optional app interaction must name an actual built/installed target and observed controls, not infer usability from compile success.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The handoff states that the image adapter buffers before its cap, does not inspect dimensions or downsample, and has no app-owned bitmap cache. Synthetic quotes are made up. Host and intercepted-service checks establish no live-feed, TLS, resource-download or device-performance behavior. The learner's modified fixture, independent schedule and recorded observations remain necessary; this answer does not complete them automatically.\u003c/p>"
