        "solution": "\u003cp>Begin with the known flow at total forty. Invalid title and 241-minute saves leave forty. The valid twenty-minute save yields forty-five. Pinning changes state/revision but not total. Deleting Blue yields Green alone at twenty-five. Keep those values in the evidence plan before interacting. The host suite supports these rules; record separate observed focus, sheet, and missing-state behavior in the scratch native target.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Choose one thousand deterministic IDs only for the larger profiling fixture. Define a fixed scroll interval, optimized build, named device, content size, repeated runs, and retained trace. If no physical device is available, leave that row pending and state what a simulator trace can contribute. Do not invent a duration to make the submission look complete.\u003c/p>\u003cp>If traces identify total reduction as material, compare a candidate cache with the invariant against recomputation after initialization, valid edit, invalid edit, deletion, and pinning. Consider the simpler alternative of reducing broad view updates. Keep the unmodified baseline for comparison and rollback. A candidate must preserve navigation identity, accessibility controls, and published values.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Submit exact commands and actual outputs, the observed or pending interaction matrix, the trace location if collected, and a decision with owner and reversal trigger. A documented no-change decision is valid when evidence finds no material bottleneck. Optional later profiling lessons extend the investigation. This answer shows a method, not a completed learner experiment or a claim of production performance.\u003c/p>"
