      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Produce your own reviewed change plan for durable synthetic saved choices, keeping implementation and integration evidence honest.",
        "steps": [
          "Run the host slice and write the values before browse, after save, and after A→B→A.",
          "Compare the existing MVVM design with the reducer example and a coordinator using at least four concrete obligations.",
          "Edit a scratch copy of ChangePlan.md with a bounded storage contract and two alternatives.",
          "Have another engineer review it when available; otherwise mark independent review pending and perform a clearly labeled author review.",
          "Rehearse a corrupted-store and failed-write recovery plan using invented records; do not claim those proposed disk tests ran.",
          "Record the native setup steps you actually completed separately from compiler and host results."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "The slice shows n1 saved in A1 and absent from the replacement session.",
          "Costs identify effect routing, lifetime, module API, and recovery work.",
          "The plan names owners, measurable acceptance, stop conditions, and data compatibility.",
          "Review identity and evidence are honest; pending independent review remains open.",
          "No provider, signed distribution, native interaction, or durable storage claim is inferred from host tests."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>A useful submission first traces one record: idle and empty path; ready with demo-a n1/n2; detail route containing S1; Saved containing n1; then demo-b S2 with empty path and membership. Returning to demo-a produces S3, and the S1 route remains rejected. Attach the gate-driven host result and identify which values were asserted.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The cost comparison keeps MVVM for the baseline. It acknowledges revision checks are distributed across models, while a reducer centralizes visible transition cases at the cost of actions and an effect runner. A coordinator makes a journey's completion and child lifetime explicit at the cost of retention and presentation bridging. None of the alternatives removes account-scoped repository policy.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The storage plan proposes a small versioned account envelope with atomic replacement and explicit errors, while retaining a prior readable representation. A corrupt read must produce a recoverable failure rather than pretending bookmarks are empty. A failed save must preserve the previous committed file. A session revoked during a write must not recreate its store. These are future adapter acceptance cases, not results from the memory fixture.\u003c/p>\u003cp>During author review, challenge whether the store can be written after revocation and whether old code can read the new envelope. Amend the contract to require a commit authority check and a tested compatibility strategy. Independent reviewer approval remains pending until someone actually supplies it. Finish with a native evidence ledger: compiled and linked adapter, Xcode target setup if performed, and actual simulator/device interactions if performed. The learner's own changes and review evidence are required; this worked plan does not certify completion.\u003c/p>"
      },
