        "remember": "A borrowed read leaves the owner available; a consuming use ends use of that binding.",
        "boundary": "The case story explains ownership, not thread scheduling. Noncopyable does not make every pointer access safe. sending follows a separate rule for crossing isolation boundaries and does not promise a deep copy. For repeating callbacks, stop registration and wait until callbacks can no longer run before releasing their context. Cancellation alone does not make that release safe."
