        "solution": "\u003cp>Add ember with symbol EMB and a distinct decimal-string price and ordered points. A local EMB query returns it; Favorites only excludes it until the save succeeds. After accepted removal, the detail route explains absence while its preference may remain. These predictions use one catalog rather than copied arrays.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Inject a writer that throws before mutation. Saved favorites and accepted rows remain unchanged with a failure message. Use separate snapshot and icon gates, invalidating only the icon; its old success/error cannot publish while the snapshot remains current. Cancellation is a request, not proof of instant remote shutdown.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Run both real service adapters through FixtureURLProtocol with an additional malformed MIME/JSON case. Record their actual outputs and rejection boundary. Those calls use intercepted local responses, not a feed. Typecheck the native source separately and create the documented target for any actual interaction.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Report buffered-cap and basic UIImage limits, absent bitmap caching/downsampling, ordinary storage evidence and pending device/provider checks. The learner's changed fixture and schedules still need implementation and recorded outcomes. This worked answer describes expected behavior without certifying copied code or unperformed native practice.\u003c/p>"
