        "solution": "\u003cp>First record the baseline compiler and the full fifteen-test result: twelve original baseline checks plus three follow-up regressions. In your scratch change, pass TTL .seconds(3) when constructing the tested repository or change its default deliberately. Accept Bridge sketch at virtual zero, advance two seconds, and check no second reader call. Advance one more second and wait for the new reader registration before supplying Garden plan. This establishes the exact three-second endpoint.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the stale failure, register both requests, return Garden plan to B, join B, then fail A with offline and join A. Browse stays ready. For Saved, hold toggle, reset the model, fail the held call, and verify failed remains false with empty notes. These schedules test current authority, rather than relying on a cancellation-friendly fake.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the additional Browse schedule, register A's delay, let B finish with Garden plan, then advance the delay and join A. Expect one reader call, ready Garden plan, and Garden plan in cache and detail. For Saved, hold a successful toggle, complete an empty reload, then release and join the toggle. The follow-up reload must display n1. Repeat with reset before the toggle completes: the old session starts no follow-up read and leaves presentation empty without failure.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The proposed envelope contains version, synthetic account identity, and bounded saved identifiers. A failed read stays a failure; a failed replacement preserves the prior committed file. Require serialized write ownership or a revocable commit lease so invalidation acknowledgment prevents future account writes. These obligations remain unexecuted until a real scratch store exists.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Conclude the ledger precisely: host logic and snippets checked; simulator source compiled/linked where supported; Xcode build and UI interactions only if you did them; independent review only if an actual person reviewed it. Record remaining gaps explicitly. The supplied reference plan and fixtures do not write course progress or pre-complete the learner's work.\u003c/p>"
