        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>List the outcomes first. Selection returns a chosen value. Cancel, completed back removal, and interactive modal dismissal return cancellation. No search matches leaves the picker open for another query. Invalid starting input is different: the caller violated this picker's input contract, so use its diagnostic and alert recovery path. Do not present that mistake as a successful search with no matches.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Each terminal path must identify who delivers the result and stops optional lookup work. Retain the dismissal adapter elsewhere because a weak delegate reference cannot keep it alive. Disable competing removal callbacks during an explicit selected-result transition and preserve the finish-once caller contract even if result storage rejects duplicates. The lesson identifies different lookup-cleanup paths in source; that is a concrete review question, not observed runtime harm. Verify with controlled pending work and focused navigation integration checks. A direct delegate invocation establishes callback handling but does not prove an actual swipe gesture completed.\u003c/p>",
