        "prompt": "Design tests that control when cancellation and overlapping requests happen. How does canceling before work starts differ from canceling while the service waits?",
        "scenario": "A model uses an injectable async service. Its current test creates a Task and immediately cancels it. A proposed overlap test waits ten milliseconds before starting request B.",
        "androidBridge": "Kotlin coroutine test schedulers and controlled fakes help establish ordering rather than wall-clock luck. Swift Task.yield and sleep are not equivalents of runTest's scheduling controls; XCTest expectations or explicit async signals must encode the event you need to observe.",
