        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Immediate cancellation can test work that begins already canceled. It cannot prove the service had started waiting. Give the fake service a start signal and a completion gate, which holds its answer until the test releases it. Start the load, wait for the signal, request cancellation, open the gate, and await the owning task. Then check the agreed state, including when the fake ignores cancellation.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For freshness, start A and observe its gate, then start B and observe B's gate. Complete B and establish its loaded result before completing A. Assert that A's late success cannot overwrite B; repeat with A failing to check the catch guard. A sleep or yield cannot establish these events reliably. Use the appropriate actor isolation for the model and asynchronous XCTest fulfillment when callback evidence is needed. Ensure every gate is released and every task is joined so no work mutates state after the assertion or hangs the test.\u003c/p>",
