        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A snapshot is an image captured under chosen conditions and compared with an accepted baseline. Compare both images before accepting a change. Check the fixture, fonts, layout timing, dimensions, appearance, scale, OS, and SDK. Decide whether the difference is intended UI behavior or changed rendering. Recording a baseline needs review; raising tolerance may simply hide a real regression.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A snapshot establishes a visual contract under those conditions. A coordinator test establishes the selected or cancelled result, while a focused UI test can verify app-level navigation and an actual gesture. Invoking the presentation delegate directly checks callback integration but does not perform UIKit's swipe transition. A stable accessibility identifier supports automation lookup; it does not establish labels, focus order, or task completion with VoiceOver. Choose the narrow additional evidence for the changed requirement, and label unexecuted checks as planned. One phone-size snapshot cannot establish large-text, localization, or tablet behavior.\u003c/p>",
