        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>async let\u003c/code> for the two known independent dashboard loads, then await both to build the dashboard. A task group fits a list whose length varies. Have each child return its input index and value. Children finish in any order, so the parent uses the index to place each result correctly. Only the parent changes the output array; the children do not share mutable output.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Seed at most three children and submit one new input after each completion frees a slot. Empty input starts none. If an error escapes the group body, remaining children are cancelled and joined, and the function throws instead of returning a partial array. Catching each child into Result would intentionally define another policy. Structured scope exit waits for its children; cancellation is cooperative rather than forced termination. The window bounds active loads, not total result memory or requests per second. Verify ordering, peak activity, failure, and cancellation with explicit fake gates.\u003c/p>",
