        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>An actor controls access to its state in separate turns. It does not hold one turn throughout an async wait. Reset can therefore run while load is suspended. Capture the account generation, the number identifying this ownership period, before waiting. After return, check cancellation and that number before committing. If it changed, throw account-changed and keep the cache empty. Keep the final check and cache update in one turn without another await.\u003c/p>\u003cp>This store rejects old success for the waiting caller too. A generalized cache might instead return an old result while refusing insertion; that is a different contract that must not be copied accidentally. Cancellation reduces wasted work, while generation validation preserves correctness even if the loader ignores it. Two concurrent loads in the same generation can still finish in either order, so this simple store does not establish latest-request-wins or coalescing. Add those policies explicitly when callers need them. Actor safety also does not override a disk framework's confinement rules or establish a transaction with a server.\u003c/p>",
