        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Give the release owner distribution containment and the client owner launch diagnosis with matching symbols. Pause further rollout where supported, while stating that a pause cannot downgrade installed build 410 or prevent every new installation. Flags cannot help code that traps before reading them. That launch defect needs a newly versioned corrective binary, built, signed, tested, and submitted through the distribution process.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the separate UI defect, compare compatible flag disablement with a binary fix and state offline or cached-configuration delays. Assign the service owner to restoring a response contract compatible with older installed clients; data changes may need forward repair. Retain the new archive, symbols, configuration, clean-install and upgrade evidence. Define resumption using confirmed task completion and diagnostics for affected cohorts, with enough volume and reporting-delay allowance. A beta upload, green CI, or release pause alone is not recovery. The runbook describes these branches and their owners without pretending that the synthetic build was distributed or repaired.\u003c/p>",
