        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A plan says what to check; an observation says what you actually found. Label the device plan and release tabletop as planned work. The source review can show a cleanup difference, not a reproduced leak or deployed repair. Executed mapper fixtures can establish their input-output rule, not faster user interaction. A shared checklist exists, but team adoption and benefit still need evidence.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For every claim, attach the method, fixture, environment, artifact, contribution, and limitation. Production performance needs the defined user boundary and representative measurements; reliability needs build, cohort, denominator, reporting coverage, and window. Reproduction needs enough setup for another engineer to investigate, yet may still leave production causality unresolved. Cross-reference the feature trace, tests, threat model, incident note, and release ledger so inconsistent assumptions surface. Use those gaps to select the next bounded responsibility and review. Neither a complete course nor a polished portfolio guarantees exhaustive iOS competence or a staff title.\u003c/p>",
