        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Choose a small owned feature with focused platform review when the gaps are device diagnosis and archive validation. Compare it with a concurrency migration's wider semantic risk and a guideline's limited benefit without adoption. Name the owner and specialist reviewers. Set two tasks: reproduce a lifecycle cancellation case with diagnostics, and validate an archive with matching symbols and an installation path. Use evidence to decide when to expand.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Gate delivery on behavior, accessibility, privacy, and release artifacts; use comparable task-outcome measures after deployment. Expand scope when independent execution and review evidence support it, rather than from a framework count. For the tabletop pre-configuration failure, assign distribution containment and a corrective binary, while preserving service compatibility for older clients; flags cannot repair that launch path. Measure team influence through reviewed adoption or reduced recurring cost, not the guideline's existence. Record planned versus observed artifacts, residual review needs, and when to reassess. This handoff owns decisions and recovery without pretending that learning exercises already produced customer outcomes.\u003c/p>",
