        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>List every source of bottom space: controller constraints, automatic scroll adjustment, explicit insets, and the hosted child's behavior. An inset is added spacing. A safe area avoids obscuring system or container UI, but does not fully describe keyboard overlap. Readable-width and margin guides serve separate horizontal purposes. Removing all safe areas may hide the gap while putting controls under system UI.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Choose one keyboard-avoidance owner. UIKit's keyboardLayoutGuide can express keyboard relationships, while a scrolling form may instead manage keyboard-aware insets and scroll the active field into view. Floating keyboards require a deliberate policy. Constrain scroll content to its content guide and viewport width appropriately so large text can grow vertically. Check child-controller containment, hosting sizing, and the specific component's safe-area contract together; a local bridge convention is not universal guidance. Verify focus, dismissal, resizing, and accessibility text in a running scratch target. A corrected inset calculation alone does not prove the field is reachable or editing state survives.\u003c/p>",
