        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A diffable snapshot lists stable item IDs and their order. Changing A's subtitle elsewhere does not necessarily configure A's cell again. Update the content lookup, then explicitly mark changed IDs that remain in the snapshot for reconfiguration. Keep A's identity unchanged. New C gets initial configuration rather than reconfiguration. Each ID must be unique across the snapshot.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Do not synthesize identity from the entire mutable display model: changing a subtitle could then look like replacing the item. Reconfiguration preserves an existing cell and does not call prepareForReuse for that update, so configuration must set every relevant visual and accessibility property. Reserve reload behavior for changes such as needing a different cell kind. Apply content and snapshot through one serialized UI owner so their updates cannot interleave incorrectly. Selection should resolve or capture A's domain ID rather than offset zero, which becomes C after insertion. Test subtitle changes, reorder, duplicate IDs, and delayed image completion separately.\u003c/p>",
