        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A frame passes through UI updates, a Core Animation commit, rendering, and display. Commit means submitting the app's changes. A commit hitch misses that app deadline. A render hitch misses a later rendering deadline despite a timely commit. A hitch disrupts continuous motion; a hang is a period of unresponsiveness, often during a discrete action. The same blocking work can contribute differently depending on when it runs.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the mapping hypothesis, select a missed commit interval and inspect relevant main-thread stacks and signposts. For the compositing hypothesis, inspect the render portion after the timely commit rather than assuming more background CPU work will help. Refresh cadence supplies deadline context, not a complete allowance for each method. Average CPU can hide a short badly timed burst. Keep gesture, content, image-cache state, text size, and device conditions fixed. After diagnosis, confirm the candidate with lighter instrumentation and the same interaction. A smooth-looking simulator pass or a print count cannot establish physical-device frame behavior.\u003c/p>",
