        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>An associated value is data carried by one enum instance. Two loaded outcomes can carry different Arrays, like two parcels carrying different contents. Raw values are fixed per declared case, so ReasonCode.offline always maps to its declared code. Unknown external strings passed to the rawValue initializer yield nil rather than adding a new case dynamically. Choose rejection, preservation or fallback deliberately instead of force unwrapping.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Loaded([]) says the work succeeded and found no names. Idle says it has not run; failed says it did not succeed. Render through an exhaustive switch and bind a loaded payload with case let. Adding a local variant then exposes missing decisions unless a catch-all hides them. The enum limits which state shapes can exist. It does not decide which transitions are allowed or whether the payload is valid. A failure message can still be blank, and successful arrays can contain duplicates unless validation says otherwise. Conformance such as Equatable or Codable is a separate capability; enum alone does not supply every desired behavior.\u003c/p>",
