        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>An Operation dependency says “wait until this other operation is finished.” It does not say “wait until it succeeds.” Finished includes cancellation and failed work, so the presenter may become ready with no report. Define a protected optional Result or a domain terminal enum: success carries a value, failure carries the supported recovery, and a stopped prerequisite cannot masquerade as a successful empty report. The graph determines when the consumer can inspect the state. The consumer must decide what that state means.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>Check that the builder does its work before its BlockOperation body returns. If it starts a callback request and immediately returns, the operation finishes too early; either use the existing async API directly or implement a correctly reviewed asynchronous Operation state machine. Keep dependencies acyclic and add them before enqueueing.\u003c/p>\n\u003cp>The feature owner should cancel obsolete operations, suppress stale publication and release retained work. Two executing operations can still leave thousands queued with retained payloads. Also limit how much work may be accepted. Test success, failure and cancellation-before-start with reversed enqueue order and controlled completion. Recover by withholding invalid publication and preserving the prior report if product policy allows, then verify cleanup before rolling the repair beyond the scratch fixture.\u003c/p>",
