        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Run three separate experiments. Change one thing at a time and state which correctness and performance limits each experiment must preserve. Launch needs a recording from process start to a defined usable endpoint. Record how installation, process state and caches were prepared. ShellConstruction and Work cannot supply presented-frame evidence. For captions, freeze Indexed, Thumb and worker count, populate the same rows and compare repeated versus cached identical text under a fixed gesture. Use a common hitch/responsiveness track, then inspect a selected missed-deadline interval for main-thread Caption attribution.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For images, keep the other controls fixed. Compare Full and Thumb using the same prepared source and the same eighty-point square display requirement. Verify dimensions, appearance and orientation, then record transient allocation and post-clear ownership separately. Host checks can establish dimensions, corrupt-source rejection and the probe ARC schedule, while phone quality and peak remain pending. Keep failures and cancellations in every experiment’s ledger. Collect a confirmation batch under matching conditions. I would name the reviewer for readiness, the memory budget owner and a rollback for each isolated change. Without those artifacts the result remains a hypothesis and executable test setup, not an improvement claim.\u003c/p>",
