        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Deleting baseline 41 removed the state needed for an upgrade test. That run checks fresh installation; upgrade verification is still pending. I request the second tester's baseline and candidate identities, device/OS, channel, preserved data setup, and exact observation. I retain raw artifacts before proposing a cause.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Compare the two artifacts’ bundle IDs, signed access groups, app-group membership, resource lookup and planned storage migration. These decide which installation and shared data each executable can access. A changed identity may create a separate installation or change access rather than erase data. I do not infer Keychain cleanup from uninstall behavior or assume a profile contains every requested claim.\u003c/p>\u003cp>I reproduce the preserved-baseline transition in an authorized scratch target using synthetic data. The owner of the affected store or entitlement boundary supplies a narrow repair and compatibility plan. Independent review checks the revised artifact and acceptance conditions; retest covers upgrade and fresh installation separately. Missing device or signing evidence stays pending. Pausing rollout stops expansion. It does not undo updates already installed.\u003c/p>",
