        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Keep closure pending until the symbols and recovery evidence match the distributed artifact. A rebuilt dSYM from the same commit may have a different image UUID, so I request the retained symbols matching the distributed binary and architecture. Fewer crashes can simply follow fewer attempts. Compare rates and outcomes for the same eligible attempts; mitigation might instead have caused people to abandon the operation.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Before comparing recovery, define which attempts are eligible, what counts as confirmed success, how cancellation is counted, the build and OS window, and diagnostic coverage. MetricKit's metric delivery is periodic and coverage is not a complete synchronous incident stream. Uploaded payload delay needs a separate collection note.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Containment can still help while diagnosis is open. Its owner must say which already installed clients it can and cannot affect. Closure needs a controlled mechanism test for the repair and comparable post-repair operational evidence. A reviewer should challenge competing explanations and missing artifacts. If those observations are unavailable, report successful containment or local regression checks only, leaving cause and recovery unverified.\u003c/p>",
