        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The widget runs in another process. That changes the ownership boundary the app-only plan assumed. An actor in the containing app cannot serialize the widget process's durable-state access. I add the widget to the eligible ledger and retain a supported old reader through an exception owned by the widget and durable-data leads.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The exception needs extra checks for old and new reader-writer combinations, interrupted writes, account separation and protected-data availability where relevant. The storage system's supported transaction or coordination mechanism must be chosen and tested; a generic actor or file lock is not a universal answer. New-format writers wait until supported readers are compatible.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Adjust funding and timing so the widget gets integration help and the temporary compatible path is maintained. An independent reviewer checks the changed ledger, recovery plan, and evidence; the updated fingerprint requires retest. The app pilot may continue within compatible bounds while removal remains pending. A review date schedules reassessment, not deletion. No fabricated adoption or outcome improvement follows from changing an exception row.\u003c/p>",
