        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Keep the parcel record as the source of truth. The Live Activity shows only a privacy-safe summary derived from it. Logout changes the owner generation, an attempt label that rejects completions from the old owner. A domain revision can reject older parcel facts, but it cannot force APNs delivery order or resurrect an activity the system ended or the person dismissed. Stale content means the estimate is old; it does not mean the parcel completed. Ending supplies a final state with an explicit dismissal policy.\n\nOn relaunch, inspect the currently tracked activities and current parcel owner. A saved activity ID does not prove that its surface is still active. If Live Activities are disabled or the activity was dismissed, preserve the ordinary in-app parcel task. Compare a regular widget or in-app status for use cases without a meaningful bounded event. Assign mobile surface recovery and server push/token ownership separately. Host policy checks cover owner and lifetime rejection; simulator rendering, device dismissal and APNs token/update behavior remain distinct evidence. Document what is still pending instead of inferring successful integration from an immutable state model.\u003c/p>",
