        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Accept valid domain changes in memory, then attempt persistence. A write failure leaves isDirty true with visible retry; reload refuses to replace those newer values. Retry saves the latest full snapshot and clears dirty only after success. If I/O becomes asynchronous, add serialized writer ownership and revision checks so an old successful write cannot mark later edits saved.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Decode version one through its dedicated representation, preserve UUIDs, completion and order, normalize the supported old names, then validate the full collection. Loading returns a migration-needed flag without overwriting original bytes. Explicit saving writes version two; a failed migration write keeps recoverable old data. Assign one store owner for this small app. Multiple scenes, large data or protected-data interruptions require coordinated storage and additional native tests. Compare a database or async actor-backed writer against the simple file's cost, and name who will verify crash, protection and upgrade behavior before extending the claim.\u003c/p>",
