        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The branches share a base containing 80, then diverge to main 60 and feature 100. Git cannot automatically choose one replacement for the same line. In this ordinary merge, unmerged index stage one is the base, stage two the checked-out main side and stage three the feature being merged. Working conflict markers expose candidate content but do not establish the desired policy.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Choose the agreed value 80, remove markers and stage the complete resolved file. Staging clears Git's unmerged entries; it does not prove policy correctness. Commit the explained resolution and verify both the final line and the two expected parents. The value can equal the original base while the merge still records both experiments. Ours and theirs name operation roles, not correct versus incorrect contributors, and rebase replay changes the context for those terms.\u003c/p>",
