        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Begin from a clean scratch snapshot and record the pre-merge tip. Inspect base and both changes, including which source, resource and configuration files jointly implement each feature. A whole-file ours/theirs choice can remove an otherwise intended addition. Resolve the product policy first, then preserve the required membership and relationships in the authoritative project or generator manifest.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Stage explicit resolved paths and verify unmerged entries are gone. Check content consistency, both integrated parents and clean status. If the choice is unclear, abort the unfinished clean-start merge and confirm the original tip/content before retrying. Actual Xcode compilation and resource lookup remain separate checks: a parsable project file or clean Git merge cannot prove packaging. The client anchor illustrates target source/dependency declarations, while this lab executes only synthetic policy conflicts and no company generator.\u003c/p>",
