        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Locate the intended old tip in the local reflog, inspect its exact file content and create a named rescue reference before further experimentation. Reflogs are local records that can expire; unreachable objects may be pruned, and lost uncommitted edits are not guaranteed to appear there. Prefer a pre-created named reference plus independent preservation for valuable uncommitted bytes.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For private owned history, restoring a selected path or reorganizing local commits can be appropriate. For accepted shared history, prepare a reviewed corrective commit or revert that preserves existing IDs. Include resources and target configuration along with source; a partial recovery can keep the packaging regression. Bind checks to the recovered candidate, name the owner of native build/resource lookup and define retry conditions. This exercise performs no remote actions or client recovery. Local reflog and scratch tests support a bounded plan, not indefinite backup or organizational approval.\u003c/p>",
