        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Build a candidate Set from saved IDs, insert pebble, encode it and call the writer. Publish the new IDs only after success. A thrown writer leaves visible favorites as luma and reports that the attempted change failed. It must not clear accepted assets, because preference and catalog ownership are independent.  On malformed JSON or an unsupported version, keep the original file. The model should leave the store unavailable and expose repair guidance rather than silently creating empty preferences and overwriting evidence. The supplied host failure closure throws before mutation; it proves that publish-after-save boundary, not every disk failure mode.  Reopening a valid temporary file verifies ordinary persistence and idempotent ID insertion. Data's atomic option supports replacement semantics but is not a complete power-loss, multi-process or multi-scene coordination proof. Record those limits and choose a migration/repair owner before broadening the store. The learner should add an independent failure case instead of copying the reference test.\u003c/p>",
