        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Each RemoteIcon owns an IconLoader and its cancellable. Loading B calls stop first, invalidating A's generation and requesting cleanup before clearing and replacing image state. When A's data or failure reaches the main-actor closure, its captured token no longer matches, so it cannot replace B or display a stale error.  The image gate is independent of the snapshot refresh gate. An icon failure affects only its placeholder; accepted asset names, prices and saved favorite choices remain usable. nil URL returns immediately, which keeps default synthetic rows free of image networking.  Start work in explicit lifecycle actions rather than body evaluation, and also handle URL changes for a still-existing row. The post-buffer encoded cap and 32-point frame do not downsample or bound decoded memory. Host gate schedules prove local relevance, while native disappearance, resource cancellation, decoding and device memory require separate observations. A direct async variant would likewise need an owned Task and post-await guards.\u003c/p>",
