        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Ship the authored companion as a bounded teaching artifact with separate evidence rows. Host checks cover validation, stale-state schedules, decimal arithmetic and preference recovery. URLProtocol executes actual Combine and async URLSession adapters against local intercepted responses. Native typechecking verifies supplied source declarations for the target. None establishes a linked or launched app.  Keep the default synthetic service, absent icon URLs and readable text controls. Require an independent Ember fixture, changed schedule and recorded acceptance output for learner completion. Runtime large text, VoiceOver, navigation behavior, optional image downloads, remote TLS/feed contracts and cancellation need actual isolated-target observations.  The image pipeline buffers before checking its encoded cap and lacks dimension inspection, downsampling and an app-owned bitmap cache. Assign those extensions an owner and representative device evidence rather than reporting a fictional performance improvement. Preserve accepted rows and saved preferences through independent failure. Later reliability and concurrency lessons are optional follow-up; the local project already explains its required HTTP and cancellation basics.\u003c/p>",
