        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The target's build label does not select its backend by itself. A configuration resource or FirebaseOptions chooses a registered app and project. The bundle ID identifies the Apple application, while the Firebase app ID identifies a Firebase registration. Inspect what the built app actually contains rather than trusting a source folder or scheme name.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Authentication supplies caller identity; Firestore or Storage rules decide whether that caller may perform the requested operation. Client configuration cannot grant Bob rights to Alice's notes. An administrative service-account credential must never be bundled to make setup convenient.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the local notebook, use the exact demo project and loopback guard, construct a named app, and route Auth, Firestore and Storage separately before their first operation. Optional remote services do not inherit those routes. Android variant experience helps reason about resources, but a Debug variant or scheme is not a server permission.\u003c/p>",
