        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Start with the host compile list: Policy.swift and Checks.swift only. Run the declared baseline and record compiler, platform and output count. A Swift parse pass of an adapter checks syntax but does not resolve Firebase imports, verify SDK signatures or produce an iOS app. A Node syntax check similarly does not execute the rules interpreter.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Prepare the target's source list, package products, deployment target, language settings and explicit gate. Exclude the host entry and optional production services. Cite the selected release's official compatibility requirements; do not invent a supported version combination or assume GoogleSignIn compatibility from Firebase alone.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Keep SDK build, simulator interaction, rules execution and remote providers as pending rows with specific required tools and acceptance cases. Starting an emulator may download a missing binary, so a CLI's presence is insufficient authorization or evidence. This report is concrete and reviewable without pretending unavailable checks passed.\u003c/p>",
