        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Treat account deletion as a workflow rather than a call followed by hiding a screen. Security-sensitive Firebase actions can require recent sign-in; recover through a deliberate reauthentication step. A stored user object is not always sufficient. Local signout, global session revocation and deleting user resources are separate decisions.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Inventory notes, Storage objects, notification associations, exports and any retained records. A trusted backend can accept a stable deletion command, preserve progress, perform bounded cleanup and record completion. Decide when identity is removed and how the worker retains authority to finish. Keep retention policy separate from the technical deletion mechanism.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Expose requested, cleanupPending, completed and retryNeeded states with a non-sensitive support reference. A retry resumes the same job and does not discard unresolved effects. The supplied notebook demonstrates session clearing and rules; it has no deployed account-deletion workflow. Required provider and server recovery observations remain pending.\u003c/p>",
