        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>isFromCache describes whether the observed result came from local cache. hasPendingWrites indicates local changes awaiting backend acknowledgement. Neither alone means a write succeeded at the server. Show those dimensions separately so a user can understand why a title is visible before the backend accepts it.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A rules denial may later reconcile a local optimistic result. Preserve the intended draft or explain the rejection instead of presenting permanent success. A server observation without pending writes is evidence about that moment, not a promise that future changes are impossible.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The notebook uses MemoryCacheSettings for local isolation, so it does not verify persisted offline behavior across restart. Its revision transaction needs a server-dependent commit and fails offline; keep that edit unsaved rather than claiming it is queued. Android cache/Flow patterns are useful analogies, but the selected SDK's metadata, persistence and transaction contracts need their own observations.\u003c/p>",
