        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Keep the live first window under a listener and historical pages under explicit one-shot query ownership. Replacing the first window should not append its every snapshot to history. A displaced row may still exist; leaving a limited result set is not deletion evidence.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Retain the last document snapshot from the same ordering and reset it when account or query shape changes. A title or reconstructed timestamp is not a robust boundary for tied values. Historical publication needs both an account stamp and page request generation, so request A's late failure cannot replace newer request B's successful state.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Merge overlapping stable IDs under the product's chosen history semantics and preserve a newer revision. The host merger does not implement Firestore ordering. Decide whether history is frozen or refreshed rather than implicitly claiming live consistency across pages. Verify composite-index readiness against the actual remote configuration; the emulator does not enforce production index requirements.\u003c/p>",
