        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A token supplies a messaging route for an installation, not proof of alert permission or current account rights. Apple delivery also involves APNs registration, entitlements and the matching backend configuration. A denied alert setting can coexist with token registration, while a stale registry can associate a current route with a previous user.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Reconcile the installation's desired account/token binding. The host plans detach Alice/t1 and attach Bob/t2, then detach Bob/t2 on signout. Server operations must be authenticated, idempotent and recoverable after lost acknowledgements. A local binding update does not prove the old server association was removed.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Treat the notification as a hint to fetch current authorized data. A tap after account change must not open Alice's cached content for Bob. Observe actual device registration, sender route and received payload separately. The supplied source performs no server send or registry write, and tokens should not enter logs, analytics properties or screenshots.\u003c/p>",
