        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Review initial collection flags before Firebase initialization, then reapply the user's stored choices for analytics, crashes and performance separately. Analytics runtime collection settings can persist and override plist defaults, so test true, revoke to false, and relaunch. Notification permission is not a substitute for any telemetry purpose decision.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Keep event names and trace attributes bounded and exclude notes, emails and tokens. Define notebook_save from repository start to return and stop it on success or error. This interval does not measure the whole app's responsiveness or prove remote upload.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For missing crash symbols, retain the exact release binary and dSYM and compare UUIDs. Same version label or a nearby Debug build is insufficient. Configure the official Crashlytics run-script inputs under a reviewed remote target, then separately observe a synthetic test crash arriving with readable symbols. Source configuration and syntax checks prove neither consent persistence nor received reports.\u003c/p>",
