        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Remote Config proposes product values; the app validates them and chooses when to activate behavior. Page size 300 is outside the lab's 1–25 range, so the host chooses the local default 10. The list rule independently caps allowed queries. A remote flag cannot safely grant administrator rights or carry a secret.\u003c/p>\u003cp>App Check supplies evidence about the app environment under the configured provider's contract. Auth identifies the user. Rules authorize the resource operation. An attested Bob still has no right to edit Alice's private note, and an authenticated Alice does not automatically prove an unmodified client environment.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Install the App Check provider factory before Firebase initialization and use metrics, supported-device observations and controlled debug integration before enforcement. A simulator debug token is not physical-device App Attest evidence. The optional remote-services source is separately gated and unexecuted, while the host only proves default selection.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Ordinary fetch failure returns validated active/default configuration with a separate diagnostic; explicit cancellation ends the operation. Firebase App Attest integration requires the signed production environment.\u003c/p>",
