        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Toggling on every drag update can repeat the action and can react to mostly vertical scrolling. Run the owner action only at an accepted onEnded completion. The pure gate requires absolute horizontal distance at least eighty and strictly greater than twice vertical distance; eighty by forty fails while minus eighty by zero passes. Check the gate on the host and actual scroll arbitration natively. Keep Pin/Unpin as a semantic button so the gesture can be removed if it conflicts. Separately, save must compare the draft's base revision zero with current revision one before publishing. Return conflict and retain the draft rather than undoing the new state. Under Reduce Motion the same actions remain valid while visual movement changes. Pin’s explicit outcome distinguishes toggled, missing, and revisionExhausted. Both Save and Pin check the next revision before candidate mutation; at Int.max they preserve the complete board. The dashboard handles a rejected Pin with a message rather than reporting success.\u003c/p>",
        "followUps": [
          "Why does a predicate pass not prove gesture delivery?",
          "When could a field-aware merge replace the conservative card revision rule?"
        ],
        "pitfalls": [
          "Committing every pointer update.",
          "Silently disabling the version check to let stale forms save."
        ]
