        "id": "iq-145-a",
        "lesson": "145",
        "level": "Senior",
        "kind": "Explain",
        "minutes": 6,
        "prompt": "Explain the smallest MVVM design for Field Notes and what Observation does within it.",
        "scenario": "Browse loads two synthetic notes and has idle, loading, ready, and failed states. A teammate wants a repository, coordinator, and reducer library before the first screen works.",
        "androidBridge": "An Android ViewModel can hold UI state, but SwiftUI Observation does not provide ViewModelStore retention or viewModelScope. Name Swift owners explicitly.",
        "rubric": [
          "Defines model, view, and view model using the actual list.",
          "Distinguishes loaded empty from never loaded.",
          "Separates Observation from MainActor isolation and cancellation.",
          "Names a stable model owner and the caller's task owner.",
          "Adds a repository only when shared data policy needs an owner."
        ],
        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Start with a Note value, a Browse view that renders state, and a view model that translates Reload and reader results into visible state. Idle means no load yet; ready with an empty array means a successful empty result. That distinction gives the screen an honest message without a collection of unrelated Boolean flags.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Observation tracks properties the view reads and changes to those properties. It does not fetch, retain the model for the desired screen lifetime, supply task scope, or reject stale responses. MainActor isolates UI-facing access, while the screen or Shell retains the model and owns the refresh task.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Keep one injected reader for the first feature. Introduce an account-scoped repository when Browse, Saved, and Detail must agree on records and membership. A reducer adds action/effect wiring; a coordinator adds journey lifetime. Both need a concrete requirement that earns those costs.\u003c/p>",
        "followUps": [
          "How would showing stale rows during refresh change the state type?",
          "What changed requirement would justify an independently testable use-case object?"
        ],
        "pitfalls": [
          "Assuming the Model suffix supplies Android lifecycle semantics.",
          "Equating Observable with concurrency safety."
        ]
